---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Contact | Kvisl" description="Official contact information for Kvisl.">
  <main class="container page-main narrow-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Contact</h1>

    <div class="policy-copy">
      <p>The official general contact address for <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> is <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>.</p>

      <div class="policy-contact-box">
        <strong>Email</strong>
        <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>
      </div>

      <h2>Editorial enquiries</h2>
      <p>For editorial questions, pitches, corrections, or factual concerns, include the relevant article title and URL where applicable. If you are requesting a correction, explain the specific statement at issue and provide reliable supporting information.</p>

      <h2>Republication and licensing</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href="/republish">Republish</a> form when possible. You may also email <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>. Republication requires written permission and a paid licence before publication.</p>

      <h2>Copyright and rights</h2>
      <p>For copyright, image rights, attribution, or other rights concerns, identify the relevant page, the material in question, your relationship to the rights, and a reliable way to contact you.</p>

      <h2>Privacy requests</h2>
      <p>For privacy requests, use the subject line “Privacy Request” and describe the request clearly. We may ask for reasonable information to verify identity before acting.</p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>If you discover a security issue, contact <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a> with enough technical detail for us to investigate. Do not access, alter, download, or retain data beyond what is necessary to demonstrate the issue.</p>

      <h2>What we will never request</h2>
      <p><span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> will never ask you to send wallet private keys, seed phrases, passwords, or authentication codes by email, form, or direct message.</p>

      <h2>Verification</h2>
      <p>Only rely on contact information and payment details published on this website. If you receive a suspicious request claiming to come from <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>, forward the details to <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a> before acting.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
